#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/vendor_runtime_module.rst:4
msgid "Vendor Runtime Module"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/vendor_runtime_module.rst:6
msgid "A Vendor Runtime Module is a :ref:`Godot module <doc_custom_modules_in_cpp>` which is only applicable at runtime in a running project. It is created like a regular :ref:`custom C++ module <doc_custom_modules_in_cpp>`, but is packaged using an :ref:`editor plugin <doc_making_plugins>` to make the functionality it provides easily accessible and usable within a *stock* Godot project."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/vendor_runtime_module.rst:13
msgid "What for?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/vendor_runtime_module.rst:15
msgid "Vendor runtime modules provide developers with access to vendor-specific optimizations, features, and/or platforms for their running projects."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/vendor_runtime_module.rst:18
msgid "This provides benefits to vendors who are able to expose their technologies to all developers, and improve and refine them in a rapid, iterative, and frictionless manner. This also provides benefits to developers and users who are able to access and use a diverse range of vendor technologies to improve their games."
msgstr ""

